Chapter: UsbKbdConnect
  cites Works chapter GopUsbKbd
  cites Works chapter GopXhci
  cites Foreword chapter Maybe

 The transport half of the USB keyboard, driven for the first time.

 `GopHid` -- the decoder that turns an 8-byte boot report into
 scancodes -- has a test (`hid-decode`). `GopUsbKbd`, which is the code
 that actually has to get that report off an interrupt endpoint, has
 never been run by anything: not by a battery, not under the emulator.
 It is the half that fails on real hardware, and it is the half nobody
 could see.

 codex-vm presents a HID boot keyboard on root port 2 whose descriptors
 are the ones this driver looks for: interface class 3, subclass 1,
 protocol 1, and an interrupt IN endpoint 0x81 at 8 bytes with bInterval
 10. Endpoint 1 IN is device context index 3 -- the same dci the real
 machine reported before going silent. So this asks the driver the
 question the hardware asks it, on a controller we can actually inspect.

 What each line proves. `connect` says the port walk, the descriptor
 walk, SET_CONFIGURATION, SET_PROTOCOL, SET_IDLE and Configure Endpoint
 all completed -- the driver got as far on the emulator as it did on the
 metal. `dci` says which endpoint it settled on. `armed` and `code` say
 whether a transfer was queued and whether a completion came back, which
 is precisely where the real machine produced nothing at all.

Section: Test

  connect-line : UsbKbd -> Text
  connect-line (k) =
    "connect: ok=" & (if k.uk-ok then "1" else "0")
      & " dci=" & show (k.uk-dci)
      & " speed=" & show ((k.uk-dev).ud-speed)
      & " slot=" & show ((k.uk-dev).ud-slot)

 Pump once to arm a transfer, then once more to check for a completion.
 The phase cell after each call says which branch the pump took, so a
 driver that never leaves idle is distinguishable from one that arms and
 hears nothing back -- two different failures that look identical from
 the outside.

  phase-of : UsbKbd -> Integer
  phase-of (k) = peek-32 (k.uk-state) 0

  opening : [Console, Device.Port, Device.Mmio] Nothing = act
    k <- kbd-connect
    print-line-uni (connect-line k)
    if k.uk-ok then act
      let p0 = kbd-pump k
      in print-line-uni ("after-arm: phase=" & show (phase-of k))
      let p1 = kbd-pump k
      in print-line-uni ("after-check: phase=" & show (phase-of k))
    end
    else print-line-uni "after-arm: SKIPPED (no keyboard)"
  end
